# production -- lean, hardened, loginnable, release. The v1.0 boot-to-getty shape.
# Note: unlike the old --production, this HAS login accounts (DEV_ACCOUNTS=y) --
# accounts no longer ride the boot-test ladder.
#
# SECURITY (dev posture): DEV_ACCOUNTS=y bakes the accounts michael + cora with
# passwords that are PUBLIC in this repo (usr/joey/joey.c DEV_*_PASS), and the
# system passphrase gating ADMIN_ELEVATE -> CAP_HOSTOWNER is public too. This is a
# development convenience, NOT a deployable posture. For a real deployment build with
# `--set DEV_ACCOUNTS=n` and provision accounts at first boot (docs/INSTALLER.md).
BUILD_TYPE=release
TESTS=n
BOOT_PROBES=n
DEV_ACCOUNTS=y
HARDENING_FULL=y
KASLR=y
SANITIZE=none
TICKLESS=y
CHUNK_GOROOT=y
CHUNK_CLADE=n
